      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T12:18:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, there is no refernce count. \nBecause its just the list of IO which qos engine keeps in the qos_export_t or qos_client_t.\nUntil and unless IO\u0027s are drained, qos_share_t or gos_client_t will not get freed.\n\nThe flow always follows : incomming request for free qos_export_t/qos_client_t -\u003e check the IO list -\u003e drain the IO in list -\u003e disable the functionality for the qos_class -\u003e free the requested qos_class.",
